// @run
// @log b
// THE RETURN RUNG OF THIS FAMILY IS CLOSED. This file was `@no-instantiate` — it ACCEPTED and
// then MISCOMPILED, `vl check` rc 0 and `vl build` reporting success while the engine refused
// the module with `type mismatch: expected (ref $type), found i32`. It now runs and prints
// `b`, and the pin is the behaviour rather than the refusal.
//
// THE DISAGREEMENT, unchanged: `ctxKeepsLitUnion` PRESERVES a literal union's members at
// `RC_ELEM` and SOFTENS them at `RC_ROOT` / `RC_FN_PARAM`, so `("a" | "b")[]` is an array of
// interned i32 ATOMS while `"a" | "b"` in a return position is a string reference. The two met
// at every read of an element: this function is emitted `(param (ref $atomArray)) (result
// (ref $string))` over a body whose `array.get` yields an i32.
//
// WHAT CLOSED IT was not the family decision this header used to say it needed. The RETURN
// BOUNDARY simply had no arm for the inline spelling: `retStrWiden` fired for `: string`, for
// `string | null` and for an inferred `string`, while an INLINE literal-union return
// (`: "a" | "b"`) was claimed by none of them — and the NAMED form (`: K`) was claimed by
// `retLitUnion`, which correctly does NOT widen because it reps as the atom. One arm, keyed on
// the seam that already separates the two forms, and the atom widens into the string slot at
// the boundary exactly as it does for `: string`.
//
// THE DECLARED-ALIAS CONTROL is still green, and now for a reason rather than by luck: it took
// the atom rep on both sides all along.
//
// THE SILENT SIBLING THIS HEADER NAMED IS STILL OPEN, and it is a DIFFERENT RUNG — a BINDING,
// not a return:
//
//   const tags: ("a" | "b")[] = ["b", "a"]
//   const v: "a" | "b" = tags[0]
//   print(v)                              // still prints `0`, the raw atom id
//
// The binding ladder's widen is keyed on `letAnnNm == "string"`, which an inline literal-union
// annotation does not spell. It remains unpinnable with the directives that exist
// (`@no-instantiate` cannot pin a valid module and `@trap` explicitly rejects it) — the same
// gap `closures/permuted-object-closure-arms.vl` records.
//
// THE GENERIC RUNG NAMED HERE IS CLOSED. This paragraph used to add "so is the generic rung:
// `tests/cases/std/xfail-miscompile-array-litunion-element.vl` still fails, one position
// further out." That file graduated — see `generic-litunion-element-read.vl` for the first
// boundary and `generic-litunion-element-bind-and-store.vl` for the last two. The BINDING
// ladder above is the residue, and it is still unpinnable.
//
// Whoever closes it should read this arm first: the fix is per-BOUNDARY, and each boundary
// has to grow the inline-spelling arm separately, because each decides its slot type in its
// own ladder.
function pick(self: ("a" | "b")[]): "a" | "b" { self[0] }

const tags: ("a" | "b")[] = ["b", "a", "b"]
print(pick(tags))
